{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1936803","formula":"Na₂ZrSi₃O₉·2H₂O","hill":"H4Na2O11Si3Zr","elements":["H","O","Na","Si","Zr"],"composition":{"H":4.0,"O":11.0,"Na":2.0,"Si":3.0,"Zr":1.0},"names":{"en":"Catapleiite","ru":"Катаплеит","uk":"Катаплеїт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Catapleiite (Na2ZrSi3O9·2H2O) is a dimorph of gaidonnayite rarely found by itself. Its name derives from the Greek words \"κατα\" (kata) and \"πλειον\" (pleion) meaning \"with more\" as it is mostly accompanied by a number of rare minerals. When pure it is colorless, but it is most often seen as a tan, brownish-red, light yellow, dark brown, flesh red or orangish in color.","ru":"Катаплеит — минерал. Название с греческого «като», «плейон» — большое количество. Образует частичные или полные псевдоморфозы по эвдиалиту.","uk":"Катаплеїт (рос. катеплеит; англ. catapleiite; нім."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1936803","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catapleiite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%97%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catapleiite-169450.jpg","license":"Public domain"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q3780191","formula":"NaCa₁₆(Si₂₃Al)O₆₀(OH)₈·14H₂O","names":{"en":"Gyrolite","uk":"Гіроліт"},"elements":["H","O","Na","Al","Si","Ca"],"fame":14,"kind":null},{